# Design: the workspace frame of a known source

## Problem

The 17 commits of 2026-11-24 sat on `f115b69`. `origin/main` had nine
more commits (the v0.7.0 release work), and two of them meet in
`internal/uploader/uploader.go`.

`9d86d67` changed `prepare`: a source with a cursor gets a probe
first, and only a source that the hub does not know is registered.
`2812eb5` sent the `sourceWorkspace` frame after the registration
acknowledgment. On the merged tree a known source never reached that
line. After an upgrade every existing source is known, so no existing
Antigravity source would send its workspace. A lookup that found
nothing at the first sync was never repeated.

Three tests of `2812eb5` failed on the merged tree before the fix, for
example "frames after a reconnect = VRFBBWVBB; want VRFBBWVRBB".

`9d86d67` also added a keepalive that calls `negotiate`, which has an
offer parameter since `2812eb5`. The merged tree did not compile.

## Approach

- The frame is sent when the hub confirms the source: after the
  registration of a new source, or after the probe of a known source.
  Both paths end in `resume`, and the frame always comes before the
  next batch.
- The cost for a known source is one round trip, and only when the
  lookup finds a path. A source that the hub stored is not looked up
  again in the process.
- `offer` holds the capability offer in one place, for the connection
  and for the keepalive.
- A merge commit holds the fix, so that each commit on `main` passes
  `make check`. A red merge with a later fix would break bisect for one
  commit.
- `main` moves by fast-forward only, so each hash in NOTES.md stays
  valid.

## Measurements

- `GOFLAGS=-count=1 make check` on the merged tree: passed twice, with
  `cmd/ohya` in 258 s and in 251 s.
- `internal/uploader` and `internal/hubsync` with the race detector:
  passed.

## Limits

- `make tla` was not rerun: neither side changed `tla/`.
- The Swift app changes of `origin/main` were not built here.
- `docs/sync-protocol.md` describes neither the keepalive nor the probe
  before the registration.
